WHY IT MOVES. L6 asserts "the per-player ink is a FORMULA, not a palette: hue = i × 137.5° at a
banded lightness". The clause it rests on — "no palette to run out of, therefore no cap" —
measured false on this paper: twelve golden-angle sticks come out at min ΔE 0.024 (r0's own
12-stick reading, re-derived by `check-peer-tin.mjs`'s ceiling search at ΔE 0.103 for FIVE
berths ≥40° apart). A formula that cannot separate twelve is not a cap-free palette; it is an
undeclared cap with no gate on it. The re-cut row asserts what is now true and is gated:
a TABLE of five sticks and five ring arms per arm, priced by `scripts/check-peer-tin.mjs`
(`lint:tin`, in CI beside `lint:ink`).

